{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-dilog-archimedean","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-dilog-archimedean","kind":"remark","title":"Archimedean realisation of $\\mathrm{Li}_2^q$ (Kirillov dilogarithm)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-dilogarithm"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-dilogarithm","tags":["hopf-algebra","dilogarithm","archimedean","q-series"],"text":"q-dilog-archimedean.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-dilog-archimedean\"></a><p>Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-dilogarithm represents the convergent Kirillov series <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_2^q(x) = \\sum_{n \\ge 1} \\frac{x^n}{n  [n]_q}</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|x| &#x3C; 1</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-dilog-archimedean.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.23.6"}
